---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArrowIcon from '../components/ArrowIcon.astro';
import { links } from '../content/links';
import { featuredPublication, previousPublications, publicationDownloads } from '../content/publications';

const questions = ['What survives?', 'What transforms?', 'What must be reinvented?'];
const workstreams = [
  'Leadership development',
  'Talent management',
  'Performance & reward',
  'Workforce management',
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Horizon Collective | Shaping the future of work"
  description="A 2–3 year movement exploring how work and organisations may evolve in the age of AI, led by thinkers and practitioners."
>
  <header class="site-header">
    <nav id="site-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a href={links.sections.movement}>
        <span class="nav-label nav-label--full">The movement</span>
        <span class="nav-label nav-label--short">Movement</span>
      </a>
      <a href={links.sections.publications}>Publications</a>
      <a href={links.sections.team}>Team</a>
      <a class="button button--small" href={links.contact.joinCollective}>
        <span class="nav-label nav-label--full">Join the collective&nbsp;<ArrowIcon /></span>
        <span class="nav-label nav-label--short">Join&nbsp;<ArrowIcon /></span>
      </a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-title" data-nav-theme="dark">
      <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="hero-lockup" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg class="hero-horiz" viewBox="0 0 271.7 58.9" focusable="false"><use href="/horizon-logo.svg#horizon-word"></use></svg>
        <div class="hero-bottom">
          <svg class="hero-zon" viewBox="228.9 0 168.8 58.9" focusable="false"><use href="/horizon-logo.svg#horizon-word"></use></svg>
          <svg class="hero-collective" viewBox="175 77 224 29" focusable="false"><use href="/horizon-logo.svg#horizon-collective"></use></svg>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1 class="sr-only" id="hero-title">Horizon Collective — a movement for the future of work</h1>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section intro" id="movement" aria-labelledby="movement-title" data-nav-theme="light">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The movement</p>
        <h2 id="movement-title">The world of work<br />is being rewritten.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p class="lead">The Horizon Collective is a 2–3 year <strong>movement</strong> where we are constantly evolving our thinking and understanding of the world of work and organisations in 7–10 years out.</p>
        <p>Through a combination of crowdsourcing from <strong>thinkers</strong> and testing these with <strong>practitioners</strong>, we develop a point of view and provide guidance about the transformation changes in the world of work, as a result of AI.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title" data-nav-theme="dark">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--lime">The questions</p>
        <h2 id="questions-title">The questions are<br />bigger than the <br class="answers-break" /><em>answers.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p>At this point in time, we are not sure exactly how the classic HR fields are going to play out. We also don’t have a view yet how L&D, Reward and some other areas are going to shape up.</p>
        <p>We also do not know yet if the employee lifecycle as a concept will survive. Maybe we need to completely reimagine and evolve all these HR areas—and understand why the speed and depth of implementation differs across companies and industries.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="question-list" aria-label="Questions we are exploring">
        {questions.map((question) => <li>{question}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <div class="art-band" aria-hidden="true" data-nav-theme="dark"></div>

    <section class="section manifesto" aria-labelledby="manifesto-title" data-nav-theme="light">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who is it for</p>
        <h2 id="manifesto-title">“A duty of care <br />for the future.”</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p>The target group for the Horizon Collective are senior HR leaders and executives in roles where they are expected to have a point of view and who feel a <strong>duty of care for the future.</strong> And who also feel the urgency and have the agency to drive this forward.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="art-band" aria-hidden="true" data-nav-theme="dark"></div>

    <section class="section work" aria-labelledby="work-title" data-nav-theme="light">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
        <h2 id="work-title">Distinct<br />workstreams.<br />One collective<br />horizon.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p>We will establish several workstreams: leadership development, talent management, performance and reward, workforce management, and more.</p>
        <p>Each workstream will have a <strong>curator</strong>; someone who will guide and facilitate the development of a point of view about a specific area. We will also invite senior academics, consultants and thought leaders to act as our <strong>council of wisdom</strong>.</p>
        <ol class="stream-list">
          {workstreams.map((stream, index) => <li><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>{stream}</li>)}
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section publication" id="publications" aria-labelledby="publication-title" data-nav-theme="dark">
      <figure>
        <a class="publication-cover-link" href={featuredPublication.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label={`Open ${featuredPublication.title} in a new tab`}>
          <img src={featuredPublication.cover.src} width={featuredPublication.cover.width} height={featuredPublication.cover.height} alt={featuredPublication.cover.alt} loading="lazy" />
        </a>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--lime">Publications</p>
        <h2 id="publication-title">A foundation <br />made to <br />evolve.</h2>
        <p>After an initial workshop in March 2026 with 25 senior HR executives, we published the first white paper. That publication captures the first thoughts and years to come, constantly evolving our thinking and understanding in a combination of crowdsourcing from <strong>thinkers</strong> and testing these with <strong>practitioners</strong>.</p>
        <p>This white paper should then serve as the starting point for that <strong>“thinking”</strong> where others can build on our ideas about <strong>“the future of”</strong> work and think of a summit and publication in 2028 when we present the final product to a wider audience.</p>
        <div class="button-row">
          {publicationDownloads.map((publication) => (
            <a
              class:list={['button', publication.style === 'light' && 'button--light']}
              href={publication.url}
              download={publication.downloadName}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              {publication.buttonLabel}&nbsp;<ArrowIcon direction="down" />
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section involvement" aria-labelledby="involvement-title" data-nav-theme="light">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Choose your level of involvement</p>
        <h2 id="involvement-title">Read.<br />Contribute.<br /><em>Shape.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="involvement-copy">
        <div class="involvement-content">
          <span class="squiggle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="body-copy">
            <p>You can decide yourself how involved you want to be. Being <strong>just a</strong> curious reader is fine, contributing to a particular workstream is fine, or anything in between. Most importantly: you should feel free and comfortable with the choices you make.</p>
            <p>We will make sure to share with you what we are working on, who the curators will be and how you can contribute. You will also ensure it all gets tied up in the collective and that we keep posting regularly about developments inside the Horizon Collective.</p>
          </div>
          <a class="button involvement-cta" href={links.contact.joinCollective}>Join the collective&nbsp;<ArrowIcon /></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="aside">Curious reader or active contributor — <em>there is no wrong way to take part.</em></p>
    </section>

    <section class="section initiators" id="initiators" aria-labelledby="initiators-title" data-nav-theme="light">
      <div class="initiators-intro">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">The initiators</p>
          <h2 id="initiators-title">Two perspectives.<br />One shared inquiry.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The Horizon Collective is a joint initiative from Robyn Agoston at <a href={links.organizations.workEvolved} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>WorkEvolved</strong></a> and Ruud Rikhof at <a href={links.organizations.brooksmiller} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>brooksmiller</strong></a>. They both have a deep interest in how the future of work and organisations are evolving and have been researching and publishing about it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="people-grid">
        <article>
          <img src="/robyn.jpeg" width="800" height="800" alt="Portrait of Robyn Agoston" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <h3>Robyn Agoston</h3>
          <p class="role">AI & Future of Work Strategist · Advisor · Speaker · Coach</p>
          <p><a href={links.people.robynLinkedIn} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Robyn Agoston</a> is an AI & Future of Work Strategist, Advisor, Speaker and Coach, working at the intersection of people and technology. She helps individuals and organisations design work for the AI era so they can make the most of both humans and AI. Over the past 20+ years, she has led digital and AI transformations across global companies like KPMG, GSK, Novartis, Beamery, Tesco, O2, Shell, BP and AstraZeneca and now with PMI. As a consultant, entrepreneur and internal adviser, she is a generalist problem-solver who thrives at blending strategic vision with practical implementation. She has a uniquely global perspective from living in seven countries, and working across Europe, Africa, Asia and North America. Change might look different in every culture, but the human elements stay surprisingly consistent</p>
          <div class="person-links" aria-label="Robyn Agoston links">
            <a href={links.organizations.workEvolved} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WorkEvolved <ArrowIcon /></a>
            <a href={links.people.robynSubstack} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Substack <ArrowIcon /></a>
            <a href={`mailto:${links.contact.robynEmail}`}>{links.contact.robynEmail}</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <img src="/ruud.jpg" width="721" height="692" alt="Portrait of Ruud Rikhof" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <h3>Ruud Rikhof</h3>
          <p class="role">Transforming HR leadership · Research · Executive search</p>
          <p>The career of <a href={links.people.ruudLinkedIn} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ruud Rikhof</a> is a blend of international HR leadership experience, research-based insight, and executive search in the Human Resources domain.
The HR career was shaped, amongst others, at IBM, Bristol-Myers Squibb, Novartis, and UBS, working globally and based out of the Netherlands, Austria, the UK, Germany, and Switzerland. In local, regional, and global positions. He was the co-founder of KennedyFitch, a recognised brand for executive search, people advisory and leadership & transformation. In parallel, he has been active in building and connecting HR communities, including as co-founder of the Beyond HR Forum.
A consistent thread in his work is research and thought leadership and he has (co-)authored several studies on the evolving role of HR and the new world of work, which continues to inform his perspective and practice. At Brooksmiller, he focuses on executive search in the HR domain. </p>
          <div class="person-links" aria-label="Ruud Rikhof links">
            <a href={links.organizations.brooksmiller} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">brooksmiller <ArrowIcon /></a>
            <a href={links.people.ruudLinkedIn} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Ruud Rikhof on LinkedIn">LinkedIn <ArrowIcon /></a>
            <a href={`mailto:${links.contact.ruudEmail}`}>{links.contact.ruudEmail}</a>
          </div>
          <div class="previous-publications">
            <p>Previous publications</p>
            <ul>
              {previousPublications.map((publication) => (
                <li><a href={publication.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{publication.title} <ArrowIcon /></a></li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="closing-title" data-nav-theme="dark">
      <h2 id="closing-title">The future of<br />work will not<br />shape <em>itself.</em></h2>
      <div>
        <p>Join us and help shape the future through ideas, research, workshops and action.</p>
        <a class="button" href={links.contact.joinCollective}>Join the conversation&nbsp;<ArrowIcon /></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer data-nav-theme="dark">
    <div class="art-band" aria-hidden="true" data-nav-theme="dark"></div>
    <div class="footer-inner" data-nav-theme="dark">
      <p>Powered by <a href={links.organizations.brooksmiller} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">brooksmiller</a> + <a href={links.organizations.workEvolved} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WorkEvolved</a></p>
      <p>© 2026 Horizon Collective</p>
      <p>Website by <a href={links.credits.monire} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Moniré</a></p>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    const revealItems = Array.from(
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('main section:not(.hero) > *')
    );
    const reducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

    revealItems.forEach((item, index) => {
      item.dataset.reveal = '';
      item.style.setProperty('--reveal-delay', `${(index % 3) * 90}ms`);
    });

    if (reducedMotion || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) {
      revealItems.forEach((item) => item.classList.add('is-visible'));
    } else {
      const revealObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
        entries.forEach((entry) => {
          if (!entry.isIntersecting) return;
          entry.target.classList.add('is-visible');
          revealObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
        });
      }, {
        threshold: 0.08,
        rootMargin: '0px 0px -8% 0px',
      });

      revealItems.forEach((item) => revealObserver.observe(item));
    }
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
